A||||5||huntleyp||Is my clutch hosed?
Z||000000||huntleyp||05-18-99||02:48 PM||||My daughters 85 GT clutch pedal is UP, but the car is not engaged...it will shift into any gear. Worn presure plate? Help!!!
Z||000001||theogre||05-18-99||05:44 PM||||sounds like the diaphram in the presure plate alright. They have a habit of spliting. most times when that happens, they won't grab enough to move the car.<p>If you are going to go to the trouble of replacing it, don't put an OEM set back in. Use something like Cenerforce, which doesn't cost much mroe than the OEM, but is a much better set. Do have the flywheel turned, even if it looks OK. You don't want to end up pulling it out again later.
Z||000002||theogre||05-18-99||05:45 PM||||also read the "clutch info uncovered" thread farther down.
Z||000003||theogre||05-18-99||05:46 PM||||that's CenterForce.....  <A HREF="http://www.centerforce.com" TARGET=_blank>www.centerforce.com</A> 
Z||000004||huntleyp||05-18-99||09:04 PM||||Thanks guy!!<br>
Z||000005||theogre||05-19-99||07:39 AM||||don't forget to make sure the slave cyl is free... tho if the pedal is full and feels close to normal it's likely ok.
